# Pairs with NoStaleAuthority. The epoch grain completes an advance without
# publishing an epoch any silo has not seen, so a delivered push supersedes
# nothing and a peer keeps trusting its old snapshot after the write returns.
MODULE: StartAdvanceKeepsKnowledge
TARGET: NoStaleAuthority
CLASS: Invariant
SUMMARY: the advance does not bump the epoch silos compare against
PERTURBS: StartAdvance

--- FIND
    /\ wstate' = "advancing"
    /\ epoch' = <<epoch[1], epoch[2] + 1>>
    /\ knows' = [t \in Silos |-> FALSE]
--- REPLACE
\* MUTATION: silos still hold the current epoch.
    /\ wstate' = "advancing"
    /\ epoch' = <<epoch[1], epoch[2] + 1>>
    /\ knows' = knows
--- END
